5.143.m:
The sage said:
Brahmins are pure all over; cows are pure all over;
goats and horses are pure from the mouth; but women are not pure anywhere!

The maiden said:
And it is not merely the appearance of these women that is delightful to embodied beings;
even embracing women brings joy and bristling delight.

The sage said:
Nor is their mere appearance delightful, but rather brings sin to the eyes;
touching a woman's body leads to destruction, and to hell after death.

5.145.m:
Sūta said:
Vṛṣadhvaja, Śarva, Mṛgavyādha as the third,
Ajaikapād, Ahirbudhnya, and Pinākin as the sixth;

5.146.m:
Sūta said:
Likewise, there is another god there who grants sons to men,
named Vaṭikeśvara, Hara who removes all sins;
